<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/"
             xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/"
             xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/"
             id="Definitions_Decision_SC_DT_02"
             name="Health supply chain traceability model and query architecture (SC-DT-02)"
             namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/dth-sc/dmn">
  <decision id="Decision_SC_DT_02" name="Health supply chain traceability model and query architecture (SC-DT-02)">
    <decisionTable id="DecisionTable_Decision_SC_DT_02" hitPolicy="FIRST">
      <input id="Input_DT02_Storage" label="Traceability data storage and aggregation topology (Ch 4 PDF pp. 54–55)">
        <inputExpression id="Input_DT02_Storage_expr" typeRef="string">
          <text>dataStorageTopology</text>
        </inputExpression>
        <inputValues>
          <text>&quot;single-shared-central-repository&quot;, &quot;hybrid-local-capture-selective-central-aggregation&quot;, &quot;distributed-stakeholder-databases&quot;</text>
        </inputValues>
      </input>
      <input id="Input_DT02_Governance" label="Traceability governance and hosting oversight (Ch 4 PDF pp. 54–55)">
        <inputExpression id="Input_DT02_Governance_expr" typeRef="string">
          <text>governanceAndOversight</text>
        </inputExpression>
        <inputValues>
          <text>&quot;central-authority-managed&quot;, &quot;collaborative-shared-governance&quot;, &quot;federated-partner-managed&quot;</text>
        </inputValues>
      </input>
      <input id="Input_DT02_Maturity" label="Supply chain partner system and network readiness (Ch 4 PDF pp. 54–56)">
        <inputExpression id="Input_DT02_Maturity_expr" typeRef="string">
          <text>partnerSystemMaturity</text>
        </inputExpression>
        <inputValues>
          <text>&quot;heterogeneous-existing-hscis&quot;, &quot;standardized-distributed-nodes&quot;</text>
        </inputValues>
      </input>
      <output id="Output_DT02_Model" label="Selected traceability model (Ch 4)" name="traceabilityModel" typeRef="string">
        <outputValues>
          <text>&quot;centralized-traceability-model&quot;, &quot;semi-centralized-traceability-model&quot;, &quot;distributed-traceability-model&quot;, &quot;unknown&quot;</text>
        </outputValues>
      </output>
      <output id="Output_DT02_Exchange" label="DHSC data exchange and query architecture" name="dataExchangeMechanism" typeRef="string">
        <outputValues>
          <text>&quot;interoperability-layer-to-central-data-warehouse&quot;, &quot;selective-event-synchronization-and-federated-query&quot;, &quot;peer-to-peer-standardized-network-exchange&quot;, &quot;unknown&quot;</text>
        </outputValues>
      </output>
      <rule id="Rule_DT02_01">
        <description>Centralized traceability model (`centralized-traceability-model`, Ch 4 Fig. 24, PDF pp. 54–55): all supply chain partners submit master, transactional, and traceability event data (what, when, where, why) through the DHSC interoperability layer to a single shared central data repository managed by a central authority (such as MOH or the national regulatory authority).</description>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_01_in_1">
          <text>&quot;single-shared-central-repository&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_01_in_2">
          <text>&quot;central-authority-managed&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_01_in_3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_01_out_1">
          <text>&quot;centralized-traceability-model&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_01_out_2">
          <text>&quot;interoperability-layer-to-central-data-warehouse&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_DT02_02">
        <description>Semi-centralized traceability model (`semi-centralized-traceability-model`, Ch 4 PDF p. 54): combines elements of the centralized and distributed models by capturing and storing operational data in stakeholder systems while synchronizing selected traceability and verification data to a shared hub.</description>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_02_in_1">
          <text>&quot;hybrid-local-capture-selective-central-aggregation&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_02_in_2">
          <text>&quot;collaborative-shared-governance&quot;, &quot;central-authority-managed&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_02_in_3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_02_out_1">
          <text>&quot;semi-centralized-traceability-model&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_02_out_2">
          <text>&quot;selective-event-synchronization-and-federated-query&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_DT02_03">
        <description>Distributed traceability model (`distributed-traceability-model`, Ch 4 PDF p. 54): each supply chain stakeholder stores traceability data locally in its own system and shares traceability data across partners through standardized peer-to-peer or networked links.</description>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_03_in_1">
          <text>&quot;distributed-stakeholder-databases&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_03_in_2">
          <text>&quot;federated-partner-managed&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_03_in_3">
          <text>&quot;standardized-distributed-nodes&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_03_out_1">
          <text>&quot;distributed-traceability-model&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_03_out_2">
          <text>&quot;peer-to-peer-standardized-network-exchange&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_DT02_04">
        <description>Where data sit in separate partner databases across heterogeneous existing HSCISs that are not yet ready for full peer-to-peer distributed networking, use the semi-centralized model via the DHSC interoperability layer (Ch 4 PDF pp. 54–56).</description>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_04_in_1">
          <text>&quot;distributed-stakeholder-databases&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_04_in_2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_04_in_3">
          <text>&quot;heterogeneous-existing-hscis&quot;</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_04_out_1">
          <text>&quot;semi-centralized-traceability-model&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_04_out_2">
          <text>&quot;selective-event-synchronization-and-federated-query&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="Rule_DT02_Unknown">
        <description>The facts do not settle the case: an input is not known, or the combination is one the handbook does not describe. Returns &quot;unknown&quot; rather than guessing (dmn-authoring, &quot;Three states belong in the table&quot;).</description>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_Unknown_in_1">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_Unknown_in_2">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="Rule_DT02_Unknown_in_3">
          <text>-</text>
        </inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_Unknown_out_1">
          <text>&quot;unknown&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="Rule_DT02_Unknown_out_2">
          <text>&quot;unknown&quot;</text>
        </outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
</definitions>
